    {
      "text": "Do you wear a watch?",
      "speaker": "a",
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 1.37
    },
    {
      "text": "Yes, I do — as a matter of fact, I can show you mine. I've worn watches since primary school, because at school I couldn't use my phone, but I still needed to know the time, so my mom bought me one. Back then it was just a simple watch — mechanical or battery-powered, just for telling the time. But now I wear a smartwatch, and it has different functions — not just time, but also heart rate. When I work out at the gym, I can see how many calories I'm actually burning, even if it's not that accurate.",
      "speaker": "b",
      "start": 1.74,
      "end": 26.7
    }
